# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Exception: the shared DEBUG keystore is committed on purpose so every
# developer's build is signed with the same certificate. Its SHA-1 is the one
# registered against the Firebase Android API key, so a fresh clone can sign
# in without each person registering their own fingerprint.
#
# This is safe: a debug keystore is not a secret (its password is the public
# default "android") and it must never be used to sign a release build.
!/debug.keystore
